<h1>Odd-Even Sort</h1>
<p>
    Odd-Even Sort functions very similarly to 
    <a href="/algorithm?id=Bubble">Bubble Sort</a>,
    in that it repeatedly walks through the array and swaps any two adjacent elements if they
    are out of order.
    <br>
    <br>
    Unlike <a href="/algorithm?id=Bubble">Bubble Sort</a>,
    Odd-Even Sort starts at the first element on the first loop, 
    the second element on the second loop,
    then alternates between starting on the first and second elements each loop.
    <br>
    <br>
    Odd-Even Sort has a similar performance to <a href="/algorithm?id=Bubble">Bubble Sort</a>,
    with a average and worst case Time Complexity of <b>n<sup>2</sup></b>.
</p>

